  ProjectName: Mower Mayhem
  ClientName: FisipGroup
  Tags: 224
  Texts:
  - category: 0
    info: Lead Developer & Team Manager
  - category: 2
    info: 'Mower Mayhem is a casual mobile racing game: clear the grass on each level
      and race to the finish line as fast as you can. It was built in Unity and shipped
      on Android and iOS.

      

'
  - category: 3
    info: 'This was a production game with a large, growing codebase that I had to
      maintain, extend and take through store release, while also leading the team
      building it.

      

'
  - category: 9
    info: "- Led the team: coordinated programmers and artists, ran Scrum with an
      incremental MVP, and was the main technical contact for the project owner.\r\n-
      Built the level pipeline: a custom Unity Editor tool so levels could be authored
      quickly without touching code.\r\n- Integrated live services:\r\n  - Analytics:
      GameAnalytics\r\n  - Ads: IronSource\r\n  - Leaderboards and in-app purchases:
      Unity Services\r\n- Kept it maintainable: careful planning, consistent testing
      and incremental feature iteration let the project keep growing without falling
      apart, all the way to release on both stores."
